Cell[TextData[{
 "This system is the clearest illustration of why v0.1.3 separates the two \
counters. Both constraints are adjoined in a ",
 StyleBox["single",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " bordering round \[LongDash] there is no intermediate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"9", "\[Times]", "9"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "379cc718-3f62-f943-9b5f-411314a64c75"],
 " stage in the recursion \[LongDash] so ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<IterationCount\>\""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->
  "42e95599-a594-fe43-98cf-179279cc87a3"],
 " is 1, ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<PassCount\>\""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->
  "84729c25-8b95-7042-a085-f519229b8002"],
 " is 2, and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<MultiplierCount\>\""], "Input",ExpressionUUID->
  "e16cce2e-aab3-c141-8b37-4b5cc4f8789e"],
 " is 2. Up to v0.1.2 the iteration counter was incremented by the number of \
new constraints and reported 2 for an object that is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{"(", "1", ")"}]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "$f^(1)$", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8be7bae4-930e-9a40-b644-d05bcad62f23"],
 ", which also consumed the iteration budget twice as fast."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9969155653002834`*^9, 3.996915579108759*^9}, {
  3.9969157289938927`*^9, 
  3.996915786209282*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3ba2e40e-9440-fb45-b405-\
9e5737c06cea"],

